# Deployment completion discipline

When this repo is open and the agent (or contributor) has **normal access** to Git push, VPS SSH, and `scripts/deploy-vps-git-archive.sh`, treat **implementation as incomplete** until production is synchronized — unless a **real blocker** is reported (permissions, build failure, migration conflict, unhealthy runtime).

## No schema ≠ no deploy

If there are **no** Postgres changes, still run the **full app deploy** when the slice changes **runtime or UI** (Next.js routes, components, API handlers, env-dependent behavior). Docs-only or comment-only edits may skip VPS if agreed, but default is: **push + deploy** so `.deploy-revision` and the live bundle stay aligned with `main`.

## Closure checklist (copy into slice report)

1. Migration check (new migration applied, or **explicit N/A**).
2. `git commit` + `git push` to authoritative branch.
3. `bash scripts/deploy-vps-git-archive.sh` from a git clone (sets `.deploy-revision` on server).
4. PM2 / process health after `scripts/deploy.sh`.
5. `GET https://nexuspro.it.com/api/health` (or project URL) → 200 after brief warm-up if needed.
6. Slice-specific production verification when relevant.
7. Mobile / device QA if UI or touch targets changed; otherwise state **pending**.
8. PASS/FAIL matrix, rollback (`DEPLOY_REF=<sha> bash scripts/deploy-vps-git-archive.sh`), remaining risks.

## Financial / persistence slices

For work touching **balances, trades, payouts, referrals, treasury**, or **new durability guarantees**: keep slices **small**, document **DB impact**, **payout impact**, and **rollback** in the report; follow `supabase-financial-integrity.mdc` and `.agents/skills/supabase/SKILL.md`. Do not mix unrelated UI refactors into the same patch.
